load @/code/type/term
  find term

load @/code/type/multiplicity
  find multiplicity

# The dependent pair type, the sigma type, the one way the theory forms a type whose second part depends on its first.
# A sigma type gathers a first type, a multiplicity, and a second type that may mention the first component. An
# ordinary pair, a product, is the special case where the second part ignores the first. A sigma also serves as an
# existential: a value of it is a witness paired with evidence about that witness.
#
# The rules. Introduction: a pair inhabits a sigma type when its first part inhabits the first type and its second part
# inhabits the second type at that first part. First projection: the first component inhabits the first type. Second
# projection: the second component inhabits the second type at the first projection. Eta: a pair rebuilt from its own
# first and second projections is the original pair (surjective pairing).
form pair-type
  link first, like term
  link usage, like multiplicity
  link second, like term
